# Local values for `astro dev` and `wrangler dev`. Copy to `.dev.vars` (git-ignored).
#
# The public pages read the site's content from the CMS (PJ-39), and the sitemap and 'view as
# user' (PJ-119) read it too, so these two are needed for every route but the static shell.
# Both are server-side secrets, declared in `astro.config.mjs`, so they never reach a browser:
#   CMS_URL=https://mc-cms.labcat.workers.dev
#   SITE_KEY=sk_…                  the vwok tenant's site key
#
# With either one empty the site serves only `/`, from its static shell, and every other path is
# a 404: a local checkout, a preview build and the Lighthouse run need no CMS.
#
# AI crawlers in robots.txt are a per-tenant setting (PJ-104): the tenant's SEO switch, default
# allow, which is vwok's legacy behaviour. This deployment switch is only read when the CMS is not
# configured at all, so a local checkout or a Lighthouse run still answers:
#   AI_CRAWLERS_ALLOWED=true
#
# The form islands (PJ-45, PJ-47) need the public Turnstile site key, whose documented test value
# always passes:
#   PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=1x00000000000000000000AA
